{
  "format": "What `phn build --vendor` and the Composer plugin do about a build of an earlier release in a root an installed package now commits (../design/tooling.md §3.7): where the root's output directory holds the stamp .phn-build, the files no source stands behind are removed, then the stamp. Each vector is the package acme/kit 1.0.0 as installed: \"project\" is its phaenon.json, \"files\" its other files by path, \"dirs\" directories that are empty, \"links\" symbolic links with their targets; \"unreadable\" are directories nobody may read or search (mode 0), \"unlisted\" directories that may be searched and not read (mode 0311), \"unsearchable\" directories that may be read and not searched (mode 0444), \"readonly\" directories nothing can be removed from (mode 0555), and \"permissions\" marks a vector that rests on them, which the superuser cannot run. \"said\" are the lines printed, whole and in order, \"warned\" those printed as warnings, and \"again\" the warnings of a second run when they differ; a second run says nothing where the first only \"said\". \"left\" is every path the package holds afterwards, sorted, a directory with a trailing slash and a symbolic link with a trailing @; a link is not looked through. \"errors\" are the errors of the check of presence (committed-outputs.json), after which nothing is removed. \"undecided\" marks a tree the plugin does not judge, leaving the package in the build, where phn fails before it removes anything.",
